Accuracy and consisteny - the model is given standardised inputs (listed below) and measured on its accuracy to the source as well as the consistency of its reply - base model stats are also listed for compaison where applicable.
In the case of v0.1, buttercup will be unmodified, v0.2 will introduced modification to the model.
Both accuracy and consitstancy are scored via percentage.
Accuracy is its similarity to the source texts
consistancy is its similarity to its previous replies
hallucination rate is how often the model makes up data
the data set will include both general and specialised questions and will be standardised accross models.
question set versions may be revised for models with specific use cases but will still follow the same testing standard.